Subject: [PATCH 05296/11362] [outer-loop] draft KAN-MILP scale stress test
 task (operator: 'digging into KAN-MILP' -> 'yes')

Investigated the 6+-week KAN-PWA/MILP formal-verification lineage (exp2051..exp5098) behind
the .467 capstone's 'exact_verifier_pivot_positive' decision. Findings:

- It's a genuinely different claim than the verifier-moat question -- exact formal bounds on
  Carnot's KAN energy model via PWA->MILP encoding + Z3, not a selection-beats-baseline claim.
- The recent result (exp5091/exp5098) is well-controlled: a real engineered-false negative
  control was correctly rejected with a counterexample, a margin-sensitive case was honestly
  left unproved, 2->3 unit composition solved cleanly.
- BUT every iteration in 6+ weeks has stayed at toy scale (2-3 units, 6-9 binary variables);
  exp2871 even fell back to brute-force enumeration rather than real MILP solving. The
  scale-boundary caveat has been repeated unchanged across 15+ experiments without ever
  testing whether MILP verification scales toward a realistic KAN model size.

Drafted a precondition-gated task in ops/known-issues.md: sweep unit count N=5..100+ (wall-
clock-bounded), re-run the FULL adversarial-rigor suite (true property + engineered-false
control + margin abstention) AT EACH N (not just the positive case), measure and honestly
report the solve-time growth curve, and identify which of the many KAN model variants
(gskan/s2kan/cikan/sos_kan/etc -- no single canonical file, corrected during drafting) is
actually production/deployed for a real comparison target. This is new work (scale never
tested), reuses the existing exp5080/5091/5098 composition pattern rather than a rewrite.

